   A compiler is a programming tool that translates high-level source code into machine code.
   An interpreter is a compiler that translates the code line-by-line.
   A JVM is a Java Virtual Machine, which is a type of compiler.
   The javac command is used for compiling Welcome.java, and the java command is ised for executing the bytecode.
   A syntax error is an error made in the creation of code, such as when a string of code is omitted or mistyped.
   A logic error is an error that results from the code performing a task other than what the programmer intended.
